  "worked_solution": "If the amount of vitamin syrup remaining is $S$ milliliters, then the rate of change of the syrup volume is $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in days.\n\nSince Tommy drinks $5$ milliliters of syrup each day, the rate of change of the amount of syrup remaining is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-5.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is negative because the amount of syrup is *decreasing*.",
